  "part": {
    "name": "Rounded rectangular perimeter frame",
    "description": "Single-piece, closed rectangular frame with a large central aperture, long straight perimeter spans, rounded corners, planar front and rear lands, an internal mating wall, and a rounded external spine. No discrete holes, bosses, fasteners, or articulated joints are present. Functional features include the central clearance opening, continuous inner locating interface, continuous planar seating or sealing lands, and impact-resistant outer edge. Structural features include the closed-loop shell, four straight rails, four rounded corner transitions, and multiple continuous fillet bands.",
    "source_views": [
      "front",
      "back",
      "left",
      "right",
      "top",
      "bottom",
      "toprightiso"
    ],
    "symmetry_note": "The in-plane rounded-rectangle profile is approximately symmetric about its horizontal and vertical centerlines. The section through the frame thickness is not fully front-to-back symmetric because the two planar lands and surrounding edge bands have different widths and radii."
  },
